# What keeps the Supabase service_role key out of the image.
#
# The build context is this directory. Docker reads this file and nothing else:
# the repository .gitignore is one level up, outside the context, and Docker
# would not read it even if it were here. Removing the file after `COPY . .`
# is not a substitute — `rm` in a later layer writes a whiteout over a layer
# that still holds the file byte for byte, and anyone who can pull the image
# unpacks it with `docker save | tar x`. A file excluded here is in no layer at
# all, which is the only version of "not in the image" that survives that.

# The four Supabase settings, service_role among them. That key is evaluated
# against no RLS policy at all, so a leaked one reads and writes every gym in
# the project. secrets.toml.example is not excluded: it carries placeholders
# and is what section 2 of the README tells you to copy.
.streamlit/secrets.toml
**/secrets.toml
.env
.env.*

# README section 2 builds the local virtualenv at streamlit/.venv, so without
# these the image would carry a second, host-built copy of every dependency
# over the one pip installed for the container's own platform.
.venv
venv

# Byte-compiled on the host, for a Python that is not necessarily this image's.
# PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE is already set, so nothing wants them.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]

# Tooling caches and editor litter. Large, machine-specific, never executed.
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
.DS_Store
